## Scope

Measure only. No file under assets/, src/, or scripts/ changed in this round. The 11 reused assets
were cut out, looked at once each, and measured from out/<asset>/stats.json. Every forge command ran
through the heavy-run load rule.

## Method

1. Read only the `variants` and `presets` block of each source (and the head note where the source
   has no variants). The rows below name a preset only where one matches the book colour.
2. Cutout at 1024 px/m on 1024x1024, front and three-quarter:
   ./forge cutout <asset> --out out/chibi-sprouts/r1/props --ppm 1024 --canvas 1024x1024 \
     --views front,three-quarter
3. Fallback when the tool reported "does not fit": out/chibi-sprouts/r1/props-large at 512 px/m.
4. Second fallback (not in the brief, see the note below): out/chibi-sprouts/r1/props-xl at 192 px/m.
5. Looked at each front cutout once; sizes read from out/<asset>/stats.json `size`.

Note on the fallback: three assets do not fit the 1024x1024 canvas at 512 px/m either. The tool
reports the canvas it needs. The brief stops at the 512 px/m fallback, so this round used a third
folder at 192 px/m, one scale for all three, and records the tool numbers as evidence. This is a
procedure gap, not an asset defect. The orchestrator decides which scale the delivery uses.

